es for Robert Pirsig's Zen and the Art of Motorcycle Maintenance, 1968-2022 (MS Am 3473). Houghton Library, Harvard University."},{"@type":"biographical/historical","#text":"Zen and the Art of Motorcycle Maintenance: An Inquiry into Values by Robert M. Pirsig was first published by William Morrow and Company in 1974. It is a work of fictionalized autobiography and the first text in which Pirsig explores his concept of \"quality\"."},{"@type":"biographical/historical","#text":"Robert Maynard Pirsig (1928-2017) was an American writer and philosopher."},{"@type":"language","#text":"In English."},{"@href":"http://id.lib.harvard.edu/ead/hou03650/catalog","#text":"Electronic finding aid available http://id.lib.harvard.edu/ead/hou03650/catalog"}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"corporate","namePart":"William Morrow and Company"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Philosophy, Modern","temporal":"20th century"}],"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Zen and the art of motorcycle maintenance : an inquiry into values"},"name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Pirsig, Robert M."}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99157175775003941/catalog"}}],"identifier":{"@type":"oclc","#text":"1419809326"},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000121904234","#text":"Houghton Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"MS Am 3473"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Houghton"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99157175775003941","processingDate":"2024-03-08T06:10Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"dacs","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"HUL"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"240119"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20240124"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"99157175775003941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)","languageOfCataloging":{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}}}},{"titleInfo":[{"title":"Zen y el arte del mantenimiento de la motocicleta","subTitle":"una indagación sobre los valores"},{"@type":"uniform","@nameTitleGroup":"1","title":"Zen and the art of motorcycle maintenance. Spanish (Valenzuela Molina)"}],"name":[{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Pirsig, Robert M.","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}}]},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Valenzuela Molina, Renato","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"translator."}}}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"sp"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Spain"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2015"},"edition":"Cuarta edición.","issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Madrid, España :"}},"publisher":"Sexto Piso,","dateIssued":"2015."}],"language":[{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"spa"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"Spanish; Castilian"}]},{"@objectPart":"translation","languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}}],"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"electronic resource"},{"@authority":"marcsmd","#text":"remote"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"computer"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"online resource"}],"extent":"1 online resource."},"abstract":{"@type":"","#text":"Fedro emprende un viaje en moto. Mientras recorren las carreteras de Estados Unidos, el arte del mantenimiento de la motocicleta pasa a ser una bella metáfora de cómo conjugar el frío y racional mundo tecnológico y el cálido e imaginativo mundo del arte. Como en el Zen, se trata de concentrarse, observar y apreciar los detalles, hasta llegar a fundirse con la propia actividad, ya sea ésta una caminata por el bosque, escribir un ensayo o tensar la cadena de una motocicleta. El viaje, entendido como el anhelo de recorrer diferentes lugares del mundo pero también como una travesía interior, sirve a Pirsig para guiarnos en las cuestiones filosóficas del arte y la técnica, el valor y la utilidad, la dialéctica y la retórica, guiado por los guiños de la carretera. "},"note":{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Robert M. Pirsig ; traducción de Renato Valenzuela Molina."},"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Pirsig, Robert M"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Fathers and sons","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Self"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"CT275.P648 ebook"},"relatedItem":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Narrativa Sexto Piso"}},{"@otherType":"Translation of:","titleInfo":{"title":"Zen and the art of motorcycle maintenance"},"name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Pirsig, Robert M."}},{"@type":"series","titleInfo":{"title":"Narrativa Sexto Piso"}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99156773572003941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9788416358328"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"841635832X"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"1382358593"}],"location":[null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99156773572003941","processingDate":"2025-06-13T01:12Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"rda","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DGITA"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"230606